#basePath	Day3

:: BeginDay
@trigger    SceneReady
@boostScore 100
@who    Astrid

$call InitUpdateMasks()
$call ToggleDeskPicture()
$call EnableDocumentClose("Day3ElijahPostcard", false)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(CoordinateInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(PhotometerInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(BlueWavelength, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(ColorInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(TemperatureInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(SpectrometerInstrument, true)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)
$call SpawnDocument("1833")

$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()
$call QueueMusic("Music.Moonthought", 3)

$call MoveToView("DocumentPuzzle")
$call SetInputState(false)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day3ElijahPostcard")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: Day3ElijahPostcardFlavor
@trigger    DocumentInspectFlip
@when   documentId == "Day3ElijahPostcard"
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} I don’t get it. We need to warn people? About what?
{@Astrid} Ugh. Elijah, I love you, but I could really use less poetry and more information. 
$call EnableDocumentClose("Day3ElijahPostcard", true, true)
$call SetInputState(true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs2
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day3ElijahPostcard"
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day3Dad")
{@Astrid} Dad... I'm so glad to hear more from him than the few little blips on the radio. 
$call SetInputState(true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs3
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day3Dad"
@interrupt
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call StartDocumentPuzzle("Day3DocumentPuzzle")
$call SetInputState(true)
{@Astrid} Has Elijah gone crazy? 

:: IncorrectDocumentResponse
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when   documentId != "1833"
@interrupt

NO.

:: CorrectDocumentResponse
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when   documentId == "1833"
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Yeah, that looks like it. $[Day3/Astrid/a_confirm_1]
$call Wait(1)

$call SetInputState(false)
$call MoveToView("Right")
$call Wait(1)

{@Dad} Astrid, this is Ursa Major. You there?

{@Astrid} Dad!

{@Dad} Sorry I've been out of touch the last few weeks. ..We have a short window to talk. 
{@Dad} I got your letter about Elijah, and all those cryptic notes you found.
{@Dad} You know, we are under so much scrutiny here to get resources for our work. 
{@Dad} We need to be on the same page with our efforts or we could be shut down.  This work really matters. 

{@Astrid} I get it, I just... I think he might have something here.

{@Dad} I know Elijah thinks this side quest is important... That kid...

{@Astrid} When do you think you're gonna be able to come home? 

{@Dad} Oh Astrid. I miss you too. The last transport back is in a few months. 
{@Dad} Hopefully I'll get through some of this work before the end of the season. 

{@Astrid} Dad! If you don't get back this season, you'll have to overwinter another year! I just can't...

{@Dad} Astrid... I'll do what I can. Time's up. I love you.

$call Wait(1)

{@Radio} CERES HQ to Station Twelve. IceCube is reading a high-energy neutrino emission from the area of the Orion Constellation.
{@Radio} Identification of nearby celestial objects is requested. Uploading area of interest...
$call WaitForMovedToView("Monitor")
$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(2)
$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@once

$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()
$call StartOpenMode()

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)

$call Wait(3)

$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()

$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(2)
$call Wait(1)
$call MonitorUI->ShowCeresLogo()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(InfraredWavelength, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(HistoricalDataInstrument, true)
{@Radio} Congratulations on being awarded clearance level 3. You are now cleared to use the historical data module.  
{@Radio} This will allow you to measure parallax over a period of time so that you can determine the distance of the stars.
{@Radio} You have also been cleared to use the infrared filter. 
{@Radio} Please reference your CERES Operator Manual for further information about your equipment.
{@Radio} Thanking you for being an important part of the CERES Distributed Network of Citizen Observatories. 
{@Radio} Together, we will map the stars for a better tomorrow.
$call MonitorUI->HideCeresLogo()
$call Wait(1)

{@Astrid} Wait, does this mean that Elijah got a satellite uplink working? Oh man, Dad is going to be so surprised. 
{@Astrid} How did he do it? 
{@Astrid} I bet he put it together out of all this old tech lying around. We used to have so much fun wiring up old radios.

//TODO
$call OpenRefGuidePage("DataTransfer")
$call Wait(1)
{@Astrid} Leo... the lion. I think I'm ready to wrestle my way through this one. 
{@Astrid} If I can just figure out this encryption key its going to really ... well, I'm not sure. 
{@Astrid} Stop the "end of the world" or something? 
{@Astrid} (*Sigh*) I can't really figure that out right now. Back to astronomy. This is pretty fun no matter what happens. 

(*typing sounds*)
$call Wait(1)
$call StartPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@cutscene
@once

$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
$call StartPuzzleMode()

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Elijah had figured out that Zosma isn’t the nearest star...
{@Astrid} Now that I've got that parallax data, I can finish what he started.
{@Astrid} From what I remember, when Earth orbits the Sun, our point of view shifts. 
{@Astrid} And when we look at a nearby star from two different positions months apart, it seems to move slightly against the background stars.
{@Astrid} That's parallax. The closer the star, the bigger the shift. The farther away it is, the smaller the shift.
{@Astrid} Now that I have this data I can figure out the distance from the stars. 
{@Astrid} We couldn'tve figured this out without years of data that was lost. 
$set temp:LeoPuzzleStarted = true
$call SetInputState(true)

:: FirstInfrared
@trigger OnLabInteraction
@when   actorId == "InfraredFilter"
@cutscene
@once

{@Astrid} Infrared filter, cool.
{@Astrid} I can't see visible light through space dust, but I can see infrared—it cuts right through. 
{@Astrid} Visible light shows the glowing stuff, but infrared is like heat vision.
{@Astrid} Wait… this one’s brightest in infrared? 
{@Astrid} That means I won’t see much in the visible wavelengths, but with the infrared filter, it should stand out.

:: LeoPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Leo"
@cutscene
@once

$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Elijah} Well… if Leo’s puzzle opened, that means the historical data made it through. Something’s working.
{@Elijah} That would mean that least part of the system’s still alive.
{@Elijah} Alright. Stay focused. Keep moving.
$call Wait(1)

$call LoadNextDay()